    summary: "曼徹斯特機場集團（Manchester Airports Group, MAG）近日曝出資料外洩事件。該機場營運商透露，駭客曾入侵其系統，竊取了位於曼徹斯特、倫敦斯坦斯德和東英格蘭的中間機場的停車場、貴賓室和快速通道預訂資料，以及機場內 Wi-Fi 註冊資訊。外洩的資料包括電子郵件地址、電話號碼、車輛登記號碼和郵遞區號。攻擊者主張透過在三個機場網站的前端 JavaScript 中留下的管理員密鑰（admin keys）進入系統。駭客團體 FulcrumSec 聲稱負責此次攻擊，並公開了約 550 GB 的未壓縮資料，據稱涉及約 870 萬至 880 萬個個體的個人資訊，包含姓名、電子郵件、電話號碼、所在城市、郵遞區和住宅 IP 位址。雖然 MAG 證實資料儲存在第三方託管的資料庫，並曾收到勒索金要求，但其營運部門未受影響。MAG 最終未支付勒索金。安全專家提醒，雖然攻擊者聲稱竊取了 MAG 平台的配置資訊，但相關細節尚未經獨立驗證。",
    tags: ["Manchester Airports Group", "MAG", "資料外洩", "勒索軟體", "FulcrumSec", "個人資料"],
    title_en: "Manchester Airports Group (MAG) Data Breach: Hackers Steal Personal Information of 8.8 Million People, Including Phone Numbers and Email Addresses",
    summary_en: "Manchester Airports Group (MAG) recently disclosed a data breach incident. The airport operator revealed that hackers had infiltrated its systems, stealing reservation data for parking, lounges, and fast-track services at intermediate airports in Manchester, London Stansted, and East England, as well as Wi-Fi registration information within the airports. The leaked data included email addresses, phone numbers, vehicle registration numbers, and postal codes. The attackers claimed they gained access to the system by leaving administrator keys in the frontend JavaScript of the three airport websites. The hacking group FulcrumSec claimed responsibility for the attack and publicly released approximately 550 GB of uncompressed data, reportedly involving personal information of 8.7 to 8.8 million individuals, including names, emails, phone numbers, cities, postal codes, and residential IP addresses. Although MAG confirmed that the data was stored in a third-party hosted database and had received a ransom demand, its operational departments were unaffected. MAG ultimately did not pay the ransom. Security experts cautioned that while the attackers claimed to have stolen configuration details of the MAG platform, these details have not been independently verified.",
    tags_en: ["Manchester Airports Group", "MAG", "Data Breach", "Ransomware", "FulcrumSec", "Personal Data"],
