    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心修復：drm/log 模組的空訊息長度邊界讀取漏洞",
    summary: "本漏洞存在於 Linux 核心的 drm/log 模組中。當呼叫 `drm_log_draw_kmsg_record()` 函式處理空訊息長度（len = 0）時，程式碼嘗試存取 `s[len - 1]` 來移除尾端換行符。由於 `len` 是無符號整數（unsigned int），當 `len` 為 0 時，減法操作會發生環繞（wraps around）至 `UINT_MAX`，導致核心執行了越界讀取（out-of-bounds read）。開發者已修復此問題，建議系統管理員應立即更新至修補了此邊界檢查的 Linux 核心版本，以防止潛在的資訊洩露或崩潰風險。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "drm/log", "out-of-bounds read", "邊界檢查", "Linux 核心更新"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Fix: Out-of-Bounds Read Vulnerability in drm/log Module",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides in the Linux kernel's drm/log module. When the function `drm_log_draw_kmsg_record()` processes a zero message length (len = 0), the code attempts to access `s[len - 1]` to remove a trailing newline character. Because `len` is an unsigned integer (unsigned int), the subtraction operation when `len` is 0 causes a wrap-around to `UINT_MAX`, resulting in an out-of-bounds read in the kernel. Developers have fixed this issue, and system administrators are advised to immediately update to a Linux kernel version that includes this boundary check fix to prevent potential information leakage or crash risks.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "drm/log", "out-of-bounds read", "boundary check", "Linux Kernel Update"],
