    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "駭客利用微軟 Teams 進行社工攻擊，透過遠端控制竊取企業高價值資產",
    summary: "駭客組織利用人為操作的入侵活動，透過微軟 Teams 的外部協作功能進行社工攻擊。攻擊者冒充 IT 或服務台人員，誘騙使用者授予互動式遠端會話權限。一旦建立遠端控制，攻擊者會使用 PowerShell 下載並靜默安裝惡意 MSI 套件，進而部署包含持久性命令執行和 C2 通訊的混淆 JavaScript 植入物。隨後，攻擊者會對主機和 Active Directory 進行廣泛偵察，並透過 Windows Remote Management (WinRM) 跨企業環境，將目標鎖定在網域控制器等高價值資產。此外，另有觀察到「Spring Ring」等大規模 Teams 語音釣魚（vishing）活動，攻擊者會誘騙受害者執行遠端監控工具，甚至升級至 NTLM relay 攻擊，目標為網域控制器。另有報告指出，The Gentlemen 勒索軟體集團展現了可重複的攻擊模式，結合了初始存取、權限提升、利用原生 Windows 工具和備份系統篡改等手段，最大化攻擊影響。這些事件凸顯了企業在遠端協作和身份驗證環節的重大安全風險。",
    tags: ["Microsoft Teams", "社工攻擊", "PowerShell", "Active Directory", "WinRM", "NTLM relay", "勒索軟體"],
    title_en: "Hackers Exploit Microsoft Teams for Social Engineering Attacks, Stealing High-Value Corporate Assets via Remote Control",
    summary_en: "Cybercrime groups are utilizing human-operated intrusion activities to conduct social engineering attacks through Microsoft Teams' external collaboration features. Attackers impersonate IT or service desk personnel, tricking users into granting interactive remote session permissions. Once remote control is established, the attackers use PowerShell to download and silently install malicious MSI packages, subsequently deploying obfuscated JavaScript implants containing persistent command execution and C2 communication. Following this, the attackers conduct extensive reconnaissance on the host and Active Directory, and then target high-value assets such as domain controllers across the enterprise environment using Windows Remote Management (WinRM). Furthermore, large-scale Teams voice phishing (vishing) activities, such as 'Spring Ring,' have also been observed, where attackers trick victims into running remote monitoring tools, even escalating to NTLM relay attacks targeting domain controllers. Another report indicates that the The Gentlemen ransomware group has demonstrated a repeatable attack pattern, combining initial access, privilege escalation, utilizing native Windows tools, and tampering with backup systems to maximize attack impact. These incidents highlight significant security risks within enterprise remote collaboration and identity verification processes.",
    tags_en: ["Microsoft Teams", "Social Engineering", "PowerShell", "Active Directory", "WinRM", "NTLM relay", "Ransomware"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Hacker News", url: "https://thehackernews.com/2026/09/threatsday-ceo-phishing-kits-5k-dropbox.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
