    id: "20260903-10535",
    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "思科（Cisco）Nexus 9000 設備曝出嚴重漏洞，可遠端執行 root 權限程式碼",
    summary: "思科發布修補程式，修復了影響 10 款基於 Silicon One 的 Nexus 9000 交換器的一個嚴重安全漏洞（CVE-2026-20212）。此漏洞的 CVSS 分數為 9.8，允許未經身份驗證的遠端攻擊者透過綁定到未受限制的 IP 位址，在預設的 Layer 3 VRF 實例中，直接連線到 TCP 埠 43210 和 43211 服務。攻擊者可透過傳送惡意輸入，以 root 權限執行程式碼，甚至可能導致設備崩潰重啟。此外，思科還發布了包含 7 個漏洞的 IOS XR 硬化版本，其中兩個漏洞的 CVSS 分數為 9.8。對於 Nexus 9000 設備，思科建議客戶升級到包含軟體維護更新（SMUs）的修補版本，或透過 iACL 阻擋目標埠，或使用 Live Protect shield 等臨時緩解措施。IOS XR 版本的漏洞則影響所有版本，建議客戶升級到包含 SMUs 的修補版本以修復記憶體安全和存取控制等問題。",
    tags: ["Cisco", "Nexus 9000", "CVE-2026-20212", "IOS XR", "交換器", "遠端程式碼執行"],
    title_en: "Cisco Nexus 9000 Equipment Exposed to Critical Vulnerability Allowing Remote Root Code Execution",
    summary_en: "Cisco has released a patch to fix a critical security vulnerability (CVE-2026-20212) affecting 10 models of Silicon One-based Nexus 9000 switches. This vulnerability has a CVSS score of 9.8 and allows unauthenticated remote attackers to connect directly to TCP ports 43210 and 43211 services within the default Layer 3 VRF instance by binding to an unrestricted IP address. Attackers can execute code with root privileges by sending malicious input, potentially leading to device crash and reboot. Furthermore, Cisco also released a hardened version of IOS XR containing 7 vulnerabilities, two of which have a CVSS score of 9.8. For Nexus 9000 devices, Cisco recommends that customers upgrade to a patched version that includes Software Maintenance Updates (SMUs), or block the target ports using iACL, or use temporary mitigations such as Live Protect shield. For the IOS XR version vulnerabilities, all versions are affected, and customers are advised to upgrade to a patched version that includes SMUs to address memory safety and access control issues.",
    tags_en: ["Cisco", "Nexus 9000", "CVE-2026-20212", "IOS XR", "Switch", "Remote Code Execution"],
