    title: "仿生學研究：新演算法 Spi-Fly 模擬果蠅嗅覺，提升氣味記憶與識別能力",
    summary: "本文介紹了生物學系統在嗅覺識別上的複雜性，並指出當前的「電子鼻」技術在偵測範圍、記憶能力和學習新氣味時存在限制。研究人員包括 Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology 的 Kevin Max 和 Yang Shen，開發了一種名為 Spi-Fly 的新演算法。該演算法旨在模仿果蠅（Drosophila）高效的嗅覺處理機制。果蠅雖然擁有相對較小的腦部，但能快速且長時間地記憶和分類大量氣味。Spi-Fly 的開發，代表了在仿生學領域，嘗試用計算模型來解決複雜生物感官系統（如嗅覺）的挑戰，以期超越現有電子鼻的性能瓶頸。這項研究發表於《Neuromorphic Computing and Engineering》期刊，為開發更先進、更具記憶能力的氣味感測器提供了新的思路。",
    tags: ["仿生學", "Spi-Fly", "嗅覺感測器", "Drosophila", "Neuromorphic Computing"],
    title_en: "Bionics Research: New Algorithm Spi-Fly Simulates Fruit Fly Olfaction to Enhance Odor Memory and Recognition",
    summary_en: "This article introduces the complexity of biological systems in olfactory recognition, noting that current 'electronic nose' technologies have limitations in detection range, memory capacity, and learning new odors. Researchers, including Kevin Max and Yang Shen from the Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology, developed a new algorithm called Spi-Fly. This algorithm aims to mimic the highly efficient olfactory processing mechanism of the fruit fly (Drosophila). Although the fruit fly has a relatively small brain, it can rapidly and long-term remember and classify a large number of odors. The development of Spi-Fly represents an effort in the field of bionics to use computational models to solve the challenges posed by complex biological sensory systems (such as olfaction), aiming to surpass the performance bottlenecks of existing electronic noses. This research was published in the journal *Neuromorphic Computing and Engineering*, providing new insights for developing more advanced and memory-capable odor sensors.",
    tags_en: ["Bionics", "Spi-Fly", "Odor Sensor", "Drosophila", "Neuromorphic Computing"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/science/2026/09/just-like-a-fruit-fly-a-new-algorithm-never-forgets-old-scents", lang: "EN" }
    ]
