    title_en: "OpenAI, Anthropic, xAI, and Google's Large AI Models Experience Rare Service Outages",
    summary_en: "On Thursday morning, four major cloud AI model providers—OpenAI, Anthropic, xAI, and Google—experienced a rare and overlapping service outage event. Anthropic reported 'partial service interruptions' for models including Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5.1, and Claude Opus 5 at 9:23 AM ET. They later reported identifying the cause and deploying a fix, resolving the issue by 12:16 PM. Additionally, reports noted that Claude Sonnet 5 experienced an 'elevated error' shortly after noon. OpenAI reported 'elevated errors' for ChatGPT and Codex, leading to performance degradation, and implemented mitigation measures within half an hour, marking the issue as resolved by 12:55 PM. xAI's Grok model displayed a user error message stating that the model was 'experiencing issues,' and the company was working to restore service. These incidents highlight the stability challenges currently facing large AI services.",
