    summary_en: "During France's tenure as G7 Chair in 2026, the French National Cybersecurity Agency (ANSSI) spearheaded the G7 cybersecurity working group. Working with member states, including the European Commission and ENISA, the group discussed the transition issues surrounding Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC). This effort builds upon the outcomes achieved during Canada's G7 Chairmanship in 2025, aiming to establish a coordinated G7 response framework. The working group issued an urgent call, emphasizing that the PQC transition has become a critical cybersecurity issue, requiring immediate action from decision-makers in both public and private sectors. Organizations, whether public or private, must plan and implement measures to transition to quantum-resistant algorithms to address the imminent quantum threat. This transition requires concerted effort from all stakeholders to ensure long-term system security.",
